-- title:
--   Fontaine's fourth step for unipotent groups over 𝒪
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\mathcal O$ a commutative ring in which $p$ is a non-zero-divisor, carrying an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $\mathbb Z/p$ whose structure map has kernel exactly $(p)$, and which is complete and separated for the $(p)$-adic topology. Let $\mathcal R$ be a commutative ring which is a cocommutative Hopf algebra over $\mathcal O$, free and finite as an $\mathcal O$-module with $\operatorname{finrank}_{\mathcal O}\mathcal R=p^a$ for some $a$, and assume the Cartier dual of its special fibre, [`CartierDual (ZMod p) (ZMod p ⊗_𝓞 ℛ)`](def/HopfAlgebra_CartierDual.html#L12) (the $\mathbb Z/p$-linear dual with its ring structure), is local. Then there are heights $h,h'\in\mathbb N$ and two towers $(L_v)_{v}$, $(L'_v)_v$ of commutative cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebras, each free and finite over $\mathcal O$, with bialgebra transition maps $t_v\colon L_{v+1}\to L_v$, resp. $t'_v$, such that every $t_v$ is surjective, $\operatorname{finrank}_{\mathcal O}L_v=p^{vh}$, the kernel of $t_v$ is [`PDivisibleGroup.Hopf.torsionIdeal 𝓞 (L (v+1)) (p^v)`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L157), namely the image of the augmentation ideal $\ker(\varepsilon)$ of $L_{v+1}$ under the $p^v$-th convolution power of the identity, and each Cartier dual of $\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}L_v$ is local (similarly for $L'$, with exponent $p^{vh'}$); moreover there are bialgebra maps $f_v\colon L'_v\to L_v$ with $f_u\circ t'_u=t_u\circ f_{u+1}$ for all $u$, an index $v$, a commutative cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebra $H$, a surjective bialgebra map $q\colon L_v\to H$ whose kernel is the ideal of $L_v$ generated by $f_v(\ker\varepsilon_{L'_v})$, and a bijective $\mathbb Z/p$-bialgebra map $\psi\colon \mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}H\to\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}\mathcal R$, such that for every $n$ and every $m$ in [`Deformation.wittHom (ZMod p) p n (ZMod p ⊗_𝓞 L v)`](def/Dieudonne_WittVectorHom.html#L246) (a truncated Witt vector of length $n$ over $\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}L_v$ that is primitive for the comultiplication) lying in [`Deformation.TruncWitt.fontaineKer p n`](def/Dieudonne_FontaineHodge.html#L76) for the inclusion $L_v\to\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}L_v$ — i.e. admitting a Witt lift $X$ over $L_v$ with ghost component $w_{n-1}(X)\in (p^n)$ — the image of $m$ under the functorial map on truncated Witt vectors induced by $\psi\circ(\mathrm{id}\otimes q)$ lies in [`Deformation.TruncWitt.fontaineKer p n`](def/Dieudonne_FontaineHodge.html#L76) for the inclusion $\mathcal R\to\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}\mathcal R$.
--
--   This is the output of the fourth step of Fontaine's classification of finite flat commutative $p$-group schemes over $W(k)$ by finite Honda systems, specialised to $k=\mathbb F_p$ and to the unipotent case: the unipotent group $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal R$ is realised, after base change to $\mathbb F_p$, as the kernel of a morphism of two unipotent $p$-divisible towers at a finite level, and Fontaine's submodule $L$ of the level maps into that of $\mathcal R$. The conclusion stops short of asserting flatness of the kernel $H$ over $\mathcal O$ or the reverse inclusion of Fontaine submodules; those are added by [`Deformation.exists_pDivisibleTower_ker_eq_map_bijective_baseChange_of_isLocalRing_cartierDual_zmodp`](thm.html#Deformation.exists_pDivisibleTower_ker_eq_map_bijective_baseChange_of_isLocalRing_cartierDual_zmodp), which cites this result.
